    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers or make your own offer. Register now at SherryFitz.ie.\n\nTi na Ri, now a well established private development, is situated on the West side of Loughrea town, just off Link road, with Gaelscoil Riabhach and Loughrea shopping complex literally within minutes walk.\n\nNo 29 is a most appealing residence, boasting a delightful interior design and layout and is presented for sale in excellent condition.\n\nViewing of this property is highly recommended and can be arranged by appointment through selling agent."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHallway - 2.28m x 4.21m\nFront aspect windows and door, understair storage, tile flooring\n\nLiving Room - 3.89m x 5.46m\nFront aspect feature bay window, insert soild fuel stove with marble surround, French doors leading to kitchen, wooden flooring\n\nKitchen Dining Room - 6.34m x 3.74m\nRear aspect window and Frech doors leading to garden, fitted wall and base units, tile flooring\n\nUtility Room - 1.91m x 2.01m\nRear aspect door, fitted wall and base units, tile flooring\n\nGround Floor wc - 1.38m x 2.00m\nRear aspect window, whb/wc, fitted storage, tile flooring\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nLanding - 1.02m x 3.14m\nHotpress/airing cupboard off, stira stairs to attic, carpet flooring\n\nBedroom 1 - 1.58m x 3.10m\nFront aspect window, wooden flooring\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.54m x 3.68m\nFront aspect feature window, wooden floor - En-Suite: 2.35m x 1.09m - Side aspect window, whb/wc/electric shower, walls partially tiled, tile flooring\n\nBedroom - 2.35m x 2.00m\nSide aspect window, whb/wc/bath with overhead shower, walls partially tiled wall, tile flooring\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.52m x 2.24m\nRear aspect window, fitted wardrobe, wooden flooring\n\nBedroom 4 - 2.67m x 3.53m\nRear aspect window, fitted wardrobe, wooden flooring\n\nGarden - \nTarmac driveway to front with side access to rear garden, patio area with garden laid to lawn, raised flower beds, shed, wall and brick boundary\n\n"
      },
